Subject: iOS: hide GPU Vertex Shading, which needs desktop GL

Upstream v3.13.0 added Video.GpuVertices ("GPU Vertex Shading" on the Video
page): meshes, rooms and models posed and transformed on the GPU. Its
renderer test, gfx_opengl_mesh_supported(), is false on gl_es, so on ANGLE's
OpenGL ES 3.0 the path never runs and the checkbox would change nothing. The
row is hidden on iOS the way overlay 0041 hides SMAA, FSR and supersampling.
The setting itself is untouched (pd.ini keeps it), and the replay/gate
comparison is unaffected: the oracle references are recorded with
Video.GpuVertices=0, which is the path iOS takes.

Every other platform is unchanged.

diff --git a/port/src/optionsmenu.c b/port/src/optionsmenu.c
index af4b39916..1d6b49c72 100644
--- a/port/src/optionsmenu.c
+++ b/port/src/optionsmenu.c
@@ -874,6 +874,12 @@ static MenuItemHandlerResult menuhandlerFramerateLimit(s32 operation, struct men
 static MenuItemHandlerResult menuhandlerGpuVertices(s32 operation, struct menuitem *item, union handlerdata *data)
 {
 	switch (operation) {
+#ifdef PLATFORM_IOS
+	case MENUOP_CHECKHIDDEN:
+		// The GPU vertex path needs desktop GL: gfx_opengl_mesh_supported()
+		// says no on gl_es, so on ANGLE's ES 3.0 the box would change nothing.
+		return true;
+#endif
 	case MENUOP_GET:
 		return videoGetGpuVertices();
 	case MENUOP_SET:
